 **Data Structures and Layout:**
-*   **Texture $I$ (RGB Triplets):** A 3D texture storing the indices and mean values. The dimensions are $D_x' \times D_y' \times D_z'$, where $D_x' = D_x/4$, $D_y' = D_y/4$, and $D_z' = D_z/4$. Each texel contains three components: $r$ (8-bit index for Codebook A), $g$ (8-bit index for Codebook B), and $b$ (mean value).
