-*   **Texture Coordinates:** GPU texture coordinates are floating-point values in the range $[0.0, 1.0]$. Integer voxel coordinates $(x, y, z)$ must be normalized to this range before sampling. For a texture of width $W$ and height $H$, the coordinate $u$ is $u = \frac{index}{W-1}$ (or similar normalization depending on hardware filtering settings) [S1].
