 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ per voxel, as decoding involves a constant number of texture lookups and arithmetic operations.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** The memory footprint is determined by the size of the compressed data: $D_x' D_y' D_z'$ triplets for indices/means, plus $256 \times 64$ entries for Codebook A and $256 \times 8$ entries for Codebook B. This is significantly smaller than the original uncompressed volume.
-*   **Performance:** The method is optimized for real-time rendering by minimizing data transfer between main memory and GPU memory. The bottleneck is the texture fetch bandwidth and the dependent texture fetches required to resolve the codebook indices.
-*   **Strengths:** High compression ratio, real-time capability on GPU hardware, portability across GPU vendors (via Cg/GLSL).
-*   **Limitations:** Limited by the fixed codebook sizes (256 entries), which may reduce accuracy for complex data distributions. The lack of bitwise operations in older GPU shading languages (like Cg) requires less efficient arithmetic alternatives.
